{"id": "EUVD-2026-82220", "enisaUuid": "5e013980-3c38-37dc-9d67-02640524088a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Require a BPF cpumask for bpf_cpumask_populate()\n\nbpf_cpumask_populate() writes to its destination with bitmap_copy(), but\nthe destination is typed as struct cpumask *. That allows the verifier to\naccept borrowed cpumask pointers returned by read-only kfuncs, such as\nscx_bpf_get_online_cpumask(), as a writable destination.\n\nMake the destination a struct bpf_cpumask * so populate follows the same\nownership rule as the other mutating cpumask kfuncs. Query kfuncs continue\nto accept const struct cpumask * inputs.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:45", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0cfc9348a045da64955af2dd6902e66dfc7d6469", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7e2a5c6519adc73be55c3de2cb545e095a0fbc5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8740156ad33be5071b588b594c55f279457f667c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8wvc-jp6j-85p4", "CVE-2026-93112"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "013a6737-dd9e-3953-acb9-c8c4afb0aa9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "950ad93df2fce70445e655ed2e74f5c1a8653ab2 <0cfc9348a045da64955af2dd6902e66dfc7d6469"}, {"id": "1c3d1782-5d7d-3e73-93a5-613a9f29bf97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "950ad93df2fce70445e655ed2e74f5c1a8653ab2 <b7e2a5c6519adc73be55c3de2cb545e095a0fbc5"}, {"id": "64970d72-a367-31a8-8181-6cc6b817fbc1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "950ad93df2fce70445e655ed2e74f5c1a8653ab2 <8740156ad33be5071b588b594c55f279457f667c"}, {"id": "794c0883-fa02-3126-8557-04e03691f5e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": 